Automatic Smart Irrigation System using Arduino Uno

Project Description

This project is an automatic irrigation system that monitors soil moisture and controls watering based on the moisture level.

When the soil becomes dry, the system activates the water pump through a relay. When sufficient moisture is detected, the pump is switched OFF.

Components Required

- Arduino Uno
- Soil Moisture Sensor
- 5V Relay Module
- Water Pump
- Jumper Wires
- Power Supply

Pin Connections

Component| Arduino Pin
Soil Sensor AO| A0
Relay IN| D3
Sensor VCC| 5V
Sensor GND| GND

Working Principle

1. The soil moisture sensor measures soil moisture.
2. Arduino reads the analog value.
3. Arduino compares the reading with a predefined threshold.
4. If the soil is dry, the pump is activated.
5. If the soil is sufficiently wet, the pump is switched OFF.

Features

- Automatic watering
- Soil moisture monitoring
- Low-cost implementation
- Standalone operation
- No internet connection required

Applications

- Home gardening
- Small agricultural fields
- Plant monitoring
- Greenhouse irrigation

Programming Language

Arduino C++

Controller

Arduino Uno

